A||||3||DXR_DAD||Is it my heater core ??
Z||000000||DXR_DAD||05-27-99||08:50 PM||||What`s up fiero guys,<p>I got in, cranked up the heat, then the defroster the whole car smelled like coolant.<br>And the windows did not defrost.<br>I didn`t see any leaks. The coolant level was fine.  What is it???
Z||000001||Gokart||05-28-99||03:41 AM||||Take a screw out of the black plastic casing up under passenger seat and see and smell for coolant. When my core went it was dripping on the floor. If it is your core, it is a fairly easy job you can do yourself. Use needle nose vise grips to clamp off both hoses from the front the front by the windsheild wiper fluid canister, which you will need to remove to get to them. New core goes for about 45.00 to 65.00. Good luck.
Z||000002||DXR_DAD||05-28-99||08:56 AM||||Thanks gokart,<p>I can see coolant on the black cover under the dash. <p>Does anyone know the GM part no. for the core<br>I hate to go to the dealer without numbers.<br>Some of those parts guys....., well you know.<p>thanks again, I will replace it today.
Z||000003||theogre||05-28-99||09:15 PM||||check the local auto parts stores first.... Heater cores are made/distributed by only a couple companies in the US, and are sold to every one. This is definatly an item you can safely shop for a good price. (Modine <br>is the name of one maker/distributor. They make nice stuff.)
